---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Eco-Design (RGESN) - Accessible UI Kit">
  <main id="main-content" class="docs-page">
    <article class="docs-content">
      <h1>Eco-Design</h1>
      <p class="lead">Building sustainable web experiences with minimal environmental impact.</p>

      <section id="why" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
        <h2 id="why-heading">Why Eco-Design Matters</h2>
        <p>
          The internet accounts for approximately 4% of global CO2 emissions — more than the
          aviation industry. Every kilobyte transferred, every computation performed, and every
          server request has an environmental cost.
        </p>
        <p>By building lighter, more efficient websites, we can:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Reduce energy consumption and carbon emissions</li>
          <li>Improve performance for all users</li>
          <li>Lower hosting and bandwidth costs</li>
          <li>Extend device battery life</li>
          <li>Make content accessible on slow connections</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="rgesn" aria-labelledby="rgesn-heading">
        <h2 id="rgesn-heading">RGESN Compliance</h2>
        <p>
          We follow the <strong>Référentiel Général d'Écoconception de Services Numériques</strong> (RGESN),
          the French reference framework for eco-design of digital services.
        </p>
        <p>Key principles we apply:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Frugality:</strong> Only include what's necessary</li>
          <li><strong>Performance:</strong> Optimize every resource</li>
          <li><strong>Durability:</strong> Support older devices and browsers</li>
          <li><strong>Transparency:</strong> Document environmental impact</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="our-approach" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
        <h2 id="approach-heading">Our Approach</h2>

        <h3>Zero JavaScript by Default</h3>
        <p>
          Most components require no JavaScript at all. When JS is needed (e.g., for dialogs), it's
          minimal and progressively enhanced.
        </p>
        <div class="stats-box">
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="stat-value">0 KB</span>
            <span class="stat-label">JS for Button component</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="stat-value">&lt; 3 KB</span>
            <span class="stat-label">CSS per component (gzipped)</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>System Fonts</h3>
        <p>
          We use the system font stack, saving 50-200 KB per page load. Users see familiar fonts
          that render instantly.
        </p>
        <pre><code>font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;</code></pre>

        <h3>CSS Custom Properties</h3>
        <p>All theming uses CSS variables — no runtime JavaScript, no CSS-in-JS overhead.</p>

        <h3>No External Dependencies</h3>
        <p>
          Zero third-party libraries for components. No npm packages to download, no supply chain to
          audit.
        </p>

        <h3>No Tracking</h3>
        <p>
          No analytics, no trackers, no third-party requests by default. Every external request has
          an environmental (and privacy) cost.
        </p>

        <h3>Static Generation</h3>
        <p>
          This site is statically generated — no server-side rendering, no database queries, no
          server computation on each request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="measurements" aria-labelledby="measurements-heading">
        <h2 id="measurements-heading">Measuring Impact</h2>

        <h3>Performance Budgets</h3>
        <p>We maintain strict performance budgets:</p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Metric</th>
              <th>Target</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Total page weight</td>
              <td>&lt; 100 KB</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>JavaScript</td>
              <td>&lt; 50 KB (gzipped)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>CSS</td>
              <td>&lt; 30 KB (gzipped)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>HTTP requests</td>
              <td>&lt; 10 per page</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Time to Interactive</td>
              <td>&lt; 2 seconds</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3>Carbon Footprint</h3>
        <p>
          You can estimate a page's carbon footprint using tools like
          <a href="https://www.websitecarbon.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >Website Carbon Calculator</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="guidelines" aria-labelledby="guidelines-heading">
        <h2 id="guidelines-heading">Component Guidelines</h2>
        <p>Each component's documentation includes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Bundle size (minified and gzipped)</li>
          <li>JavaScript requirement (if any)</li>
          <li>Lighter alternatives when available</li>
          <li>Performance considerations</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="resources" aria-labelledby="resources-heading">
        <h2 id="resources-heading">Resources</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://ecoresponsable.numerique.gouv.fr/publications/referentiel-general-ecoconception/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">RGESN (French)</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.thegreenwebfoundation.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >The Green Web Foundation</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.websitecarbon.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >Website Carbon Calculator</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://sustainablewebdesign.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >Sustainable Web Design</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.w3.org/community/sustyweb/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >W3C Sustainable Web Design Community Group</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .docs-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .docs-content h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-4xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .docs-content section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .docs-content h2 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .docs-content section:first-of-type h2 {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .docs-content h3 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .docs-content p {
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .docs-content ul {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-left: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .docs-content li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .stats-box {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  .stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .stat-value {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-success);
  }

  .stat-label {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  pre {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  code {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  th {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
  }
</style>
